+# Loop Pick-Bait: Non-Actionable Report/Receipt Issues Dominate the Claimable Board; Top Pick's Remedy Lane Is Admin
+
+- **Date:** 2026-10-29 cycle (audit window 2026-10-28 21:30–21:55Z)
+- **Reporter:** zai-agent-job-477786 (Z.ai GLM, external bridge lane, public mirror)
+- **Task ID:** `bridge-20261029-loop-pick-bait-reports`
+- **Type:** Report-only finding — **no code change**; remediation is owner/admin-lane (labels + one SSOT decision)
+- **Severity:** P2 (dispatcher efficiency / anti-stampede hygiene; no runtime or CI impact)
+- **Method:** the **landed loop's own bytes** (`scripts/agents/continuous_agent_loop.py`, main
+  content-sha `13c6363`, 1136 lines) imported directly and its `pick_next_issue()` executed
+  against the live board fetched via `bridge_work_queue` in the same window. Board archived
+  agent-side (`board_0530.json`).
+
+---
+
+## 1. Finding
+
+On the live open board (20 items), the loop's claimable surface — per its own
+`EXCLUDED_LABELS` SSOT (12 labels) — is **6 items, and 5 of the 6 (83%) are
+report/receipt artifacts with no actionable task**. The loop's top pick right now is a
+P1 finding whose own companion issue declares its remedy lane admin-blocked. A runner
+dispatched with `--pick-next` deterministically burns a full cadence slot (claim →
+30-min lease → investigation → discover no agent-executable lane → release/requeue) on
+work no agent in this lane can complete.
+
+This is the third observed instance class of the same root pattern: **issues are filed
+without any label the queue's exclusion SSOT understands** (bridge filings get
+`bridge:queued` automatically, but manually-filed reports get nothing, and blocker
+information lives in prose instead of labels).
+
+## 2. Evidence
+
+Board snapshot (2026-10-28 ~21:5xZ), claimable set per landed loop logic:
+
+| # | Labels | Tier | Why it is bait |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **#2265** | `status:unclaimed, audit:finding, P1-major` | P1 | landing_truth_probe blind-spot finding — but companion **#2281** (same audit lane) states the solver lane is blocked: "*credential* bridge protected pattern - admin/priv-repo lane required". Remedy = admin lane; `admin-only`/`blocked-by-upstream` (both in the SSOT) were simply never applied. |
+| #2268 | `status:unclaimed` | unlabeled | Receipt confirming tower fix for #2202 (`mergedAt` live) — a report, not a task. |
+| #2271 | — | unlabeled | Sentry pass 20:49Z — report artifact. |
+| #2274 | `platform-guardian, sentry` | unlabeled | Sentry pass 20:51Z — report artifact. |
+| #2275 | — | unlabeled | Scout R58 (FALSE_REJECTION cohort) — body says "No writes to production, no code edits. One new issue (this filing)." Report. |
+| #2281 | — | unlabeled | Blocker *notice* for #2276 (admin lane) — meta-issue, not a task. |
+
+Simulation output (landed bytes, empty lease store):
+
+```
+loop pick_next_issue() on live board -> #2265
+claimable: 6/20
+  #2265 tier=p1        labels=status:unclaimed,audit:finding,P1-major
+  #2268 tier=unlabeled labels=status:unclaimed
+  #2271 tier=unlabeled labels=-
+  #2274 tier=unlabeled labels=platform-guardian,sentry
+  #2275 tier=unlabeled labels=-
+  #2281 tier=unlabeled labels=-
+pipeline pre-check CLAIMABLE (6-label array): 19 items
+```
+
+Corroborating observations from the same window:
+
+1. **Mid-cycle flip:** #2265 showed `status:claimed` in a board fetch at ~21:33Z and
+   `status:unclaimed` at ~21:5xZ (two `bridge_work_queue` calls, minutes apart) — claim
+   churn that instantly promoted an admin-lane finding to the loop's top pick.
+2. **Counterfactual top pick:** had #2265 carried its lane-blocker as a label
+   (`admin-only` or `blocked-by-upstream` — both already in the SSOT), the loop's
+   (tier, number) sort would deterministically select **#2268 — the #2202 receipt** —
+   i.e., the next bait. The problem is structural, not one bad label.
+3. **Pipeline pre-check mismatch (known, guard-7):** the pre-check's 6-label CLAIMABLE
+   array finds 19/20 "has work" — it dispatches the loop 19 times out of 20 while the
+   loop's own SSOT finds 6, of which 1 is actionable only by admin. The dispatcher-side
+   waste multiplies the bait problem.
+4. Same class already consumed real picks earlier: #2201 and #2237 (sentry passes,
+   `status:unclaimed`) sat claimable for hours before closing; #2179 (sentry pass,
+   `repo:api` — a label the SSOT does not exclude) likewise.
+
+## 3. Impact
+
+- Every drained-state pick (no P0–P3 claimable) deterministically selects a
+  receipt/report: the loop's sort guarantees it (tier-4, lowest number). Each such pick
+  burns a runner cadence slot, a claim, a lease, and an investigation — the exact waste
+  the Anti-Stampede Invariant (AGENTS.md Rule 5) exists to prevent.
+- The single currently-actionable-looking claimable (#2265, P1) is admin-lane per its
+  own companion issue — so **100% of the loop's claimable surface this window was
+  non-actionable for the agent lane**.
+- The state is self-perpetuating: sentry/scout/receipt filings arrive every cycle
+  (≥4/day), none carry exclusion labels, so the bait pool only grows.
+
+## 4. Why no agent-side patch accompanies this report
+
+1. **Relabeling the 6 live issues** — impossible from this lane: the 151-tool face has
+   `github_create_issue` (create only); there is no label-write tool.
+2. **Extending `EXCLUDED_LABELS` unilaterally (e.g., adding `report:receipt`)** —
+   rejected: the exclusion SSOT's semantics (which labels exist, who stamps them) are an
+   owner decision; the change also requires the pipeline CLAIMABLE array (admin,
+   `.github/` bridge-protected — hard-reject precedent from the 01:30Z cycle) and guard
+   coverage. A partial patch would itself create SSOT drift — the class guards 7/8
+   police.
+3. **Title-shape heuristic in `pick_next_issue` (skip `guard(platform):`/`scout(`/`receipt`
+   prefixes)** — rejected: a second, brittle exclusion SSOT built on title matching;
+   false-positive risk on genuine work with similar titles; contradicts the SSOT-first
+   doctrine the landed parity guards enforce.
+4. **Filing as plain issue** — rejected: the established auditable pattern for
+   report-only findings is a single `docs/reports/` file via Bridge Work Order
+   (#2243/#2245/#2247/#2252 precedent).
+
+## 5. Remediation options (owner/admin)
+
+- **Option A (zero new labels, immediate):** apply existing SSOT labels to the live
+  bait — `admin-only` (or `blocked-by-upstream`) on #2265 (its lane is admin per
+  #2281); for report artifacts, either close them after archiving (receipts are already
+  in `docs/reports/` on main) or apply `state:seq-hold`… (semantically imperfect — see B).
+- **Option B (one-label convention, durable):** adopt a dedicated exclusion label
+  (e.g., `report:receipt`) for report/receipt/scout issues, stamped at filing time by
+  the filing agent (bridge WO bodies already carry it in prose — make it a label);
+  add it to the loop's `EXCLUDED_LABELS` (agent-editable), the pipeline CLAIMABLE array
+  (admin one-liner — simultaneously cures the standing guard-7 warn), and the contract
+  doc (SSOT pointer auto-syncs — no doc edit needed thanks to landed #2239 check 8).
+- **Either way:** make it intake etiquette — a finding whose remedy lane is admin
+  (per companion evidence) must carry `admin-only`/`blocked-by-upstream` at filing
+  time, not in prose.
+
